From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:22:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] webservices: errors, text conversions, float/decimal, faults,
 field mappings, channel types (3201)

Batch for the webservices gap-A items (82): WS_ERROR is filled when a call fails;
every text type converts to every other; binary float/decimal records and
appending to a binary text node; WS_FLOAT/DECIMAL/VOID types; NO_FIELD and
XML_ATTRIBUTE field mappings; unhandled attributes fail a struct read unless
ignored; SOAP 1.1/1.2 faults read and write; fault error header property;
endpoint address headers in messages; more channel and listener types; TCP
binding template. Invalid options, mappings and moves answer E_INVALIDARG.

Gate fastwebsvc2 (149 checks), 19 mutants SG_MUTANT_WS2_* each shown caught.
webservices conformance tests pass on 64 and 32 bit. Guessed values and the
open types are listed in patches/notes/3201.txt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

